{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-15877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{5}^{8}\\frac{-4}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-15877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x-4.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 5 & 8 \\\\ u & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{8}\\frac{-4}{(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{-4}{u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{-4}{u}\\,\\text{d}u & =-4{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-15877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5e922a0d552b89c78c6638b78463c35ff1741f9cf20d8a374be7fa31e5c62be"} {"question" "q-15877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-15877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-15877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-49622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the definite integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/4}\\sqrt{8x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-49622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =8x+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=8x+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ u & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}\\sqrt{8x+1}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}({3}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}({({3}^{3})}^{1/2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(3\\sqrt{3}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-49622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5e922a0d552b89c78c6638b78463c35ff1741f9cf20d8a374be7fa31e5c62be"} {"question" "q-49622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-49622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{12}(3\\sqrt{3})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}(3\\sqrt{3}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}(3\\sqrt{3}+1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{7}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}(3\\sqrt{3}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-49622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}(3\\sqrt{3}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6x}{\\sqrt{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{2}+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6x}{\\sqrt{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u & ={-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{u}}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =6-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =6-3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5e922a0d552b89c78c6638b78463c35ff1741f9cf20d8a374be7fa31e5c62be"} {"question" "q-336745" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336745" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-3\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{(9x+2)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =9x+2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =9 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=9x+2.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ u & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{(9x+2)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{2}^{5}{u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{(9x+2)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}({5}^{3}-{2}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}(125-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5e922a0d552b89c78c6638b78463c35ff1741f9cf20d8a374be7fa31e5c62be"} {"question" "q-336783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2\\sqrt{2}}2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{2}+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({9}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(({3}^{2})^{3/2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({3}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5e922a0d552b89c78c6638b78463c35ff1741f9cf20d8a374be7fa31e5c62be"} {"question" "q-336804" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"} {"question" "q-336804" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{52}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030922/state.json" "file_sha256" "6756097989a07412cd7cefd4e188c562ee3863c4fb463dd6e5a738702d168d19"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1209 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
